ule Data Block","quantity":1},{"name":"RMA70-12","quantity":4},{"name":"LMD","quantity":20000}]},{"stage":"Stage 2","attributesIncreased":"HP +130 , DEF +30","effectLabel":"Glistening improved","effectText":"All Vanguard Operators recover 28 HP per second while this unit is deployed","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":1},{"name":"Data Supplement Stick","quantity":15},{"name":"Polyester Pack","quantity":5},{"name":"LMD","quantity":25000}]},{"stage":"Stage 3","attributesIncreased":"HP +150 , DEF +35","effectLabel":"Glistening improved","effectText":"All Vanguard Operators recover 30 HP per second while this unit is deployed","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":1},{"name":"Data Supplement Instrument","quantity":5},{"name":"Compound Cutting Fluid","quantity":6},{"name":"LMD","quantity":30000}]}]}],"review":{"official":"Myrtle is a\nDurin\n. She has insisted that her previous job title be recorded as: Generalissimo.\nHer appearance and temperament are somewhat childish, but on the battlefield, she displays considerable enthusiasm and knack for command. She is able to boost\noperator\nmorale while at the same time, providing them treatment. She is totally reliable.","editor":null,"rating":null},"synergies":[],"techniques":[{"technique":null,"techniqueDescription":null,"description":null}],"guides":[],"stats":{"phases":[{"elite":0,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":45,"base":{"hp":658,"atk":231,"def":138,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":8,"block":1,"interval":1.3},"max":{"hp":902,"atk":331,"def":193,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":8,"block":1,"interval":1.3},"rangeId":"1-1"},{"elite":1,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":60,"base":{"hp":902,"atk":331,"def":193,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":10,"block":1,"interval":1.3},"max":{"hp":1142,"atk":436,"def":255,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":10,"block":1,"interval":1.3},"rangeId":"1-1"},{"elite":2,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":70,"base":{"hp":1142,"atk":436,"def":255,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":10,"block":1,"interval":1.3},"max":{"hp":1565,"atk":520,"def":300,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":10,"block":1,"interval":1.3},"rangeId":"1-1"}],"trust":{"hp":0,"atk":0,"def":50}},"files":[{"section":"Clinical Analysis","unlock":"Unlocked at 25 trust","description":"Imaging tests reveal clear, normal outlines of internal organs, and no abnormal shadows have been detected. Originium granules have not been detected in the circulatory system and there is no sign of infection. At this time, this operator is believed to be uninfected.\n\n[Cell-Originium Assimilation] 0%\nMyrtle shows no signs of Oripathy infection.\n\n[Blood Originium-Crystal Density] 0.12u/L\nMyrtle very rarely comes into contact with Originium.\n\nMyrtle's physical examination indicators are all standard."},{"section":"Archive File 1","unlock":"Unlocked at 50 trust","description":"This Durin girl is full of energy.\nBecause she previously lived only underground, she is very curious about the world up here.\nShe likes group operations and likes to be where everyone else is. Some of the older operators show a deep fondness for her."},{"section":"Archive File 2","unlock":"Unlocked at 100 trust","description":"Durin brought Myrtle back to the base one day, completely unannounced. According to Durin, she suddenly felt a burst of 'inspiration' while she was sleeping. She went out for a walk and found Myrtle.\nRegardless of whatever it was that inspired Durin, Myrtle's proved to be a fully capable Rhodes Island operator. She had also expressed a desire to find work. Thus, through means no one quite understood, Rhodes Island added a new operator to our ranks.\nIn addition, the reason Myrtle left her homeland is similar to that of many of the Durins who come above ground - she was simply looking for a new life."},{"section":"Archive File 3","unlock":"Unlocked at 150 trust","description":"Somewhat regrettably, Myrtle's induction into Rhodes Island has not yet resulted in any greater understanding of the underground world.\nIn fact, despite the many Durin who have come up from the underground world, their descriptions have never given us any real impression of what it's like down there.\nPerhaps the underground world is too large.\nAnyway, the addition of Myrtle is not without its benefits. At the very least, she has reversed everyone's impressions of the Durin people. After all, up until now, Durin had let us believe that most Durins are lazy and sleep all the time."},{"section":"Archive File 4","unlock":"Unlocked at 200 trust","description":"The most noteworthy thing about Miss Myrtle is the apple that she always carries in her hand. While it may appear to be an ordinary apple at first glance, her combat style reveals that it is much more than that.\nAfter soliciting my advice for their studies, Rhodes Island researchers were surprised to find extremely complex but precise structures inside the apple that can transform to most efficiently release Miss Myrtle's powers.\nThis design is becoming more popular as a form of expression, conceptually similar to how Casters will channel their Arts through mediums that they are most comfortable with. However, this apple differs subtly from these more 'popular' forms.\nAccording to a researcher who has long been obsessed with making Arts-related devices, the mechanism behind this apple felt as if it was derived from 'faith.'"}]},"appearances":[{"label":"Base","iconPath":"/four-star-icons/Myrtle%20-%20Base.webp","fullPath":"/four-star-skins/Myrtle%20-%20Base.webp"},{"label":"Elite 2","iconPath":"/four-star-icons/Myrtle%20-%20Elite%202.webp","fullPath":"/four-star-skins/Myrtle%20-%20Elite%202.webp"},{"label":"Bustling Festival","iconPath":"/four-star-icons/Myrtle%20-%20Bustling%20Festival.webp","fullPath":"/four-star-skins/Myrtle%20-%20Bustling%20Festival.webp"},{"label":"Light Gold Celebration","iconPath":"/four-star-icons/Myrtle%20-%20Light%20Gold%20Celebration.webp","fullPath":"/four-star-skins/Myrtle%20-%20Light%20Gold%20Celebration.webp"},{"label":"Summer Flowers FA062","iconPath":"/four-star-icons/Myrtle%20-%20Summer%20Flowers%20FA062.webp","fullPath":"/four-star-skins/Myrtle%20-%20Summer%20Flowers%20FA062.webp"}],"skinObtainByLabel":{"Bustling Festival":"18 OP","Summer Flowers FA062":"18 OP"},"synergyMatches":[],"autoSynergyGroups":[{"name":"Rhodes Island","type":"faction","entries":[{"operatorName":"Closure","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Closure%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":true,"badges":[{"label":"T2","skillIconPath":null,"talentLabel":"T2","sourceText":"Minimum DP -4 ( -1 ) when Closure is in the squad; all [Rhodes Island] Operators ATK +4%.","matchedKeyword":"Rhodes Island"}]},{"operatorName":"Kal'tsit - Esperanta","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Kal'tsit%20-%20Esperanta%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":true,"badges":[{"label":"T2","skillIconPath":null,"talentLabel":"T2","sourceText":"When other allies enter this unit's Attack Range, they will immediately gain 1 Shield and be granted a buff, healing by 60 ( +10 ) HP per second for 30 seconds (This effect is unable to be stacked and the healing effect is doubled for [Rhodes Island] Operators).","matchedKeyword":"Rhodes Island"}]},{"operatorName":"Angelina the Mellow Wish","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Angelina%20the%20Mellow%20Wish%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Ascalon","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Ascalon%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Blaze","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Blaze%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Blaze the Igniting Spark","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Blaze%20the%20Igniting%20Spark%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Ceobe","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Ceobe%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Ch'en the Dawnstreak","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Ch'en%20the%20Dawnstreak%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Ch'en the Holungday",